WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.699 --> 00:00:05.350
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.170
- We are trying McDonald's
in Israel right now.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:10.150
- I'm not a huge, huge burger person,

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.133
so I think it'll be better kosher.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:13.890
- I'm a pretty big
McDonald's fan in general.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:14.948
I think it's the best of the fast food.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:17.531
(upbeat music)

00:00:22.995 --> 00:00:24.230
- We do not have this in America.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:26.670
- They look a little bit
like mini mozzarella sticks.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.480
- Inside there's corn and
mashed potatoes or something?

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.490
- I'm a little worried,

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:32.330
'cause it has real corn pieces in it.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.163
- I love corn.

00:00:33.163 --> 00:00:34.700
I (beeping) will eat corn bread all day.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:35.950
It's sweet and savory,

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:37.850
and I'm a big sweet and savory person.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:38.733
- Those are pretty good.

00:00:38.733 --> 00:00:40.470
- This is really gross.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:41.850
- It tastes kind of like a tofu nugget.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:42.830
I wonder what's inside,

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:44.210
'cause I don't think it's cheese.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.043
- It's a little bland.

00:00:45.043 --> 00:00:45.876
- I have no clue what this is.

00:00:45.876 --> 00:00:47.649
- I'm trying the Texas sauce.

00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:48.604
- It smells like barbecue.

00:00:48.604 --> 00:00:51.998
- So this is what
Israelis think Texans eat.

00:00:51.998 --> 00:00:53.190
It's pretty accurate.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.280
It tastes like barbecue sauce.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:55.518
- Those are seriously really good.

00:00:55.518 --> 00:00:57.050
(upbeat music)

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.430
I'm trying the MyMac Chicken.

00:00:58.430 --> 00:00:59.717
- Is it a Big Mac or a MyMac?

00:00:59.717 --> 00:01:00.750
- [Woman] It's a MyMac Chicken.

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:01.860
- Israel is a tech country.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:03.497
It's like iMac, MyMac.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:04.995
- [Woman] This is as big as my face.

00:01:04.995 --> 00:01:05.870
- It's (beeping) huge.

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:07.850
- It looks really similar to what we have,

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:09.440
but it has the tahini sauce on it.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:10.660
And everything fell out.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:12.563
- It's got two crispy chickens in it.

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:15.690
- It tastes like a
chicken tender on a bun.

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:17.430
You don't really taste the tahini sauce.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.630
- We really know how to do
fried chicken in America.

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:21.160
This fried chicken's crispy and nice,

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:23.793
but it's not like fried chicken, you know?

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:24.956
Kind of bland, actually.

00:01:24.956 --> 00:01:27.539
(upbeat music)

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:31.540
- This is apparently what
Israelis think Americans

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.040
eat all the time because this is called

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.830
the Mega Big America.

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.360
- Las Vegas edition.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:37.460
I am from Las Vegas.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:38.513
- A very big patty.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:39.923
Okay.

00:01:40.026 --> 00:01:41.330
- This type of meat here
looks like an entire steak

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:43.520
and it's got kinda weird
granular stuff going on.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:47.117
- It has tomatoes, lettuce, pickle, onion.

00:01:47.722 --> 00:01:49.000
It kinda smells like a veggie patty.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.139
- It smells just like meat, honestly.

00:01:51.139 --> 00:01:53.130
- This'll be good. (laughing)

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:55.393
I'm not a big meat eater, but that's good.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:56.910
It's really thick, too.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:58.733
- Oh my God.

00:01:58.750 --> 00:01:59.893
It's super dry.

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:01.000
- Super well done.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.450
- The texture of the
meat's kind of somewhere

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:03.800
between hamburger and steak.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:05.150
- Great (beeping) tomatoes.

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:08.020
- Israeli McDonald's, good to go.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.590
- Israeli McDonald's was
more or less the same

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:10.770
as the American McDonald's.

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:11.603
- Pretty good.

00:02:11.603 --> 00:02:12.610
Just like regular McDonald's.

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:13.710
- I would definitely get these again.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:15.210
Corn sticks, they're the best.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:19.003
- I give it A+, minus the corn sticks.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.150
- Would eat, if it
weren't for all the other

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:22.251
great food in this earth.

00:02:22.251 --> 00:02:24.834
(upbeat music)

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.784
- Hey, Unsolved is on a new channel.

00:02:33.784 --> 00:02:35.140
- [Unison] Subscribe here.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:36.233
- That was my part.

